## Scenarios

### flat pool codec decode cost

#### decodes a large escape-free text pool in well under the pre-fix cost

- Verify: decodes a large escape-free text pool in well under the pre-fix cost
   - Expected: decoded.len() equals `2000`
   - Expected: decoded[0] equals `chunk`
   - Expected: decoded[1999] equals `chunk`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 19 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: decodes a large escape-free text pool in well under the pre-fix cost")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
# 2000 values x 400 chars = 800k characters that the old loop walked
# one slice-and-concat at a time. An unescaped value decodes to itself,
# so the only correct amount of work here is a scan.
var chunk = "abcdefghij"
while chunk.len() < 400:
    chunk = chunk + "abcdefghij"
var pool: [text] = []
while pool.len() < 2000:
    pool = pool.push(chunk)
val blob = flat_pool_enc_text(pool)
val t0 = rt_time_now_unix_micros()
val decoded = flat_pool_dec_text(FlatPoolReader.new(blob))
val elapsed_ms = (rt_time_now_unix_micros() - t0) / 1000
expect(decoded.len()).to_equal(2000)
expect(decoded[0]).to_equal(chunk)
expect(decoded[1999]).to_equal(chunk)
expect(elapsed_ms < 5000).to_be_true()
```

</details>

#### decodes an escaped text pool in bulk, not one character at a time

- Verify: decodes an escaped text pool in bulk, not one character at a time
   - Expected: decoded.len() equals `2000`
   - Expected: decoded[0] equals `chunk`
   - Expected: decoded[1999] equals `chunk`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 20 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: decodes an escaped text pool in bulk, not one character at a time")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
# Escapes miss the identity fast path, so this pins the OTHER half of the
# fix: the two escape forms are rewritten by three bulk runtime replaces
# rather than by an interpreted per-character loop.
var chunk = "alpha\nbeta\\gamma"
while chunk.len() < 400:
    chunk = chunk + "alpha\nbeta\\gamma"
var pool: [text] = []
while pool.len() < 2000:
    pool = pool.push(chunk)
val blob = flat_pool_enc_text(pool)
val t0 = rt_time_now_unix_micros()
val decoded = flat_pool_dec_text(FlatPoolReader.new(blob))
val elapsed_ms = (rt_time_now_unix_micros() - t0) / 1000
expect(decoded.len()).to_equal(2000)
# Fidelity first: a fast decode that loses an escape is worthless.
expect(decoded[0]).to_equal(chunk)
expect(decoded[1999]).to_equal(chunk)
expect(elapsed_ms < 5000).to_be_true()
```

</details>

#### returns an escape-free value unchanged, byte for byte

- Verify: returns an escape-free value unchanged, byte for byte
   - Expected: flat_pool_unescape("") equals ``
   - Expected: flat_pool_unescape("plain identifier") equals `plain identifier`
   - Expected: flat_pool_unescape("n not an escape") equals `n not an escape`
   - Expected: flat_pool_unescape("a\\nb") equals `a\nb`
   - Expected: flat_pool_unescape("a\\\\b") equals `a\\b`
   - Expected: flat_pool_unescape("\\") equals `\\`
   - Expected: flat_pool_unescape("a\\qb") equals `a\\qb`
   - Expected: flat_pool_unescape("\\\\n") equals `\\n`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 15 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: returns an escape-free value unchanged, byte for byte")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
# The fast path is only sound because the encoder emits a backslash
# ONLY as the lead byte of an escape. Pin that it is identity, not an
# approximation: a value that merely LOOKS escaped after decoding
# would be a silent miscompile.
expect(flat_pool_unescape("")).to_equal("")
expect(flat_pool_unescape("plain identifier")).to_equal("plain identifier")
expect(flat_pool_unescape("n not an escape")).to_equal("n not an escape")
# And the slow path still handles the adversarial shapes.
expect(flat_pool_unescape("a\\nb")).to_equal("a\nb")
expect(flat_pool_unescape("a\\\\b")).to_equal("a\\b")
expect(flat_pool_unescape("\\")).to_equal("\\")
expect(flat_pool_unescape("a\\qb")).to_equal("a\\qb")
expect(flat_pool_unescape("\\\\n")).to_equal("\\n")
```

</details>

#### decodes i64 and nested list pools without a per-element reader call

- Verify: decodes i64 and nested list pools without a per-element reader call
   - Expected: decoded.len() equals `300000`
   - Expected: decoded[299999] equals `299999 * 7 - 3`
   - Expected: decoded_lists.len() equals `60000`
   - Expected: decoded_lists[1] equals `[1, 2]`
   - Expected: decoded_lists[3].len() equals `0`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 34 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: decodes i64 and nested list pools without a per-element reader call")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
# doc/08_tracking/bug/frontend_cache_hit_restore_cost_2026-08-22.md
# A real compiler module's entry is several hundred thousand lines
# (hir_codec.spl: 573k, 383k in the expr pools), and until 2026-08-22
# every one of them went through next() -> next_i64() ->
# flat_pool_parse_i64() plus a fresh inner decode call per AST node's
# list, which under the interpreter cost more than the decode itself:
# a cache HIT on hir_codec.spl restored in 24-31 s, i.e. most of a
# real parse, and 8 HIR shard children each paid it for all 687
# modules. Decoding 300k i64 values took 11.4 s the old way and 2.6 s
# with the cursor loop inlined; this bound sits well above the new
# cost on a loaded box and well below the old one.
var pool: [i64] = []
var lists: [[i64]] = []
var i: i64 = 0
while i < 300000:
    pool = pool.push(i * 7 - 3)
    if i < 60000:
        lists = lists.push(if i % 3 == 0: [] else: [i, i + 1])
    i = i + 1
val blob = flat_pool_enc_i64(pool) + flat_pool_enc_i64_list(lists)
val r = FlatPoolReader.new(blob)
val t0 = rt_time_now_unix_micros()
val decoded = flat_pool_dec_i64(r)
val decoded_lists = flat_pool_dec_i64_list(r)
val elapsed_ms = (rt_time_now_unix_micros() - t0) / 1000
expect(decoded.len()).to_equal(300000)
expect(decoded[299999]).to_equal(299999 * 7 - 3)
expect(decoded_lists.len()).to_equal(60000)
expect(decoded_lists[1]).to_equal([1, 2])
expect(decoded_lists[3].len()).to_equal(0)
expect(r.ok).to_be_true()
expect(elapsed_ms < 6000).to_be_true()
```

</details>

#### marks the reader not-ok on a truncated inner list instead of reading past the blob

- Verify: marks the reader not-ok on a truncated inner list instead of reading past the blob
   - Expected: lists.len() equals `1`
   - Expected: lists[0] equals `[7]`
   - Expected: r.ok is false


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 8 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: marks the reader not-ok on a truncated inner list instead of reading past the blob")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val blob = "2\n1\n7\n5\n"   # two lists; the second claims 5 items but has none
val r = FlatPoolReader.new(blob)
val lists = flat_pool_dec_i64_list(r)
expect(lists.len()).to_equal(1)
expect(lists[0]).to_equal([7])
expect(r.ok).to_equal(false)
```

